C. Qualitative Results
More qualitative detection results are illustrated in Fig. 4. Fig. 4 (a) shows the annotated ground truth, (b) is the detection results for CenterPoint based on raw point cloud without using any painting strategy. (c) and (d) show the detection results with 2D painted and 3D painted point clouds, respectively, while (e) is the results based on our proposed framework. As shown in the figure, there are false positive detection results caused 2D painting due to frustum blurring effect, while 3D painting method produces worse foreground class segmentation compared to 2D image segmentation. Instead, our FusionPainting can combine two complementary information from 2D and 3D segmentation, and detect objects more accurately.
